{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487063118,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDk2MTAwNDY1OQ=="},"added":["question"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487063559,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY0OTg2Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-279649863"},"message":"Important implication: plain Git repos have no (cached) metadata.\n\nBut I don't see a bad cost/benefit ratio when turning a plain git repo into an annex repo, at the point where metadata is desired.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1487065046,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY1NjIwMA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-279656200"},"message":"\u003e - superdataset authors must be able to filter out undesired metadata on\n\u003e  aggregate, e.g. disable by metadata source\n\nMay be not only \"by metadata source\" but even key-based or sth. like that? I don't think it's important to fully implement right now, but would be nice to allow for it by design.\n\n\u003e But I don't see a bad cost/benefit ratio when turning a plain git repo into an annex repo, at the point where metadata is desired.\n\nI agree.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487065776,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTY1OTY3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-279659670"},"message":"\u003e May be not only \"by metadata source\" but even key-based or sth. like that?\n\nBy-source is actually based on a key in the current implementation. The difficulty is that metadata has an arbitrary structure and it is difficult to express filters robustly. The technicalities are much simpler.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1487140053,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTkyODExOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-279928119"},"message":"Important implication: metadata aggregation upwards in the hierarchy becomes impossible when there is one plain git repo in the chain.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1487170072,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4MDAzMDA0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-280030048"},"message":"\u003e But I don't see a bad cost/benefit ratio when turning a plain git repo into an annex repo, at the point where metadata is desired.\n\nThe only benefit I would see would be if there is a file to attach meta-data to, so effectively making those repos \"full fledged\" annex repos with some content requiring annex supported hosting.  I guess I will grasp it better as things evolve ;)","files":null},{"type":2,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1490522338,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE3OlJlbmFtZWRUaXRsZUV2ZW50MTAxNTYyNDc2MA=="},"title":"RF: metadata layout, storage, aggregation, and access procedure","was":"RF: metadata layout, storage, aggregation, and access procedure"},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1490522348,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDEwMTU2MjQ3Nzk="},"added":["feedback-desired"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1490522348,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTAxNTYyNDc4MA=="},"added":[],"removed":["question"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1490526454,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4OTI3MzA3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-289273075"},"message":"@bpoldrack @yarikoptic Top comment has growing description of new metadata concept. Please chime in if you feel like it.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1490536598,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI4OTI4NjI0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-289286248"},"message":"thanks for the buzz.  I will try to get through it soon(ish).  yet thinking about leaking concern as well","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1491200443,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5MTA1NzcxNA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-291057714"},"message":"Unless I hear from you @yarikoptic @bpoldrack otherwise, I will start implementing this proposal.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1491230110,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5MTE2MjA0Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-291162047"},"message":"0. `I am debating whether to change the storage concept for metadata from custom\nfiles with JSON-LD content to JSON-LD metadata values in annex's keystore. `\n- at first I thought that it would lead to only cons e.g.\n  - inability to publish it to non-annex-compatible portals, e.g. github\n  - loosing the benefit of git compressing its objects, thus providing efficient updates to those possibly long .json files.  Every update then would require fetching entire possibly growing in size file(s)\n- but in general I do not mind I guess, if we indeed start to aggregate even summaries of per-file meta-data which would lead to higher chance to leak meta-data\n1.\n```markdown\n    - `.datalad/meta/info`: JSON file providing basic properties for all aggregated metadata files in the store (see next). This file is always present, even when no subdatasets exist.\n        - **Basic dataset metadata is attached to this file using `git annex metadata`**. We might need to include some info on subdatasets in here too, in order to have useful minimal metadata for subdatasets after \"`git clone`\"\n        - Basic dataset metadata of **subdataset** could be aggregated into the **content** of this file in a superdataset\n```\n- I am not entirely clear about ideas of this concept (\"volatile\" `.datalad/meta/info` file also with aggregated meta-data), but if I got it right I see following scalability issue:  annex will assign those aggregated fields to the 'key' of that meta-data file.  If that file to change more or less frequently, its key would be changing, meta-data would need to be duplicated/expanded for the the new key.  Might lead to explosion of the amount of storage you would need for `git-annex` branch even though many keys (one per aggregation) there then would carry copies of the aggregated meta-data.  I guess git's compression of objects would mitigate it to a good degree, but still not sure if there would be no significant impact as the history of the dataset grows.  Altogether I do not see much of positive use for adding `annex metadata` to that file, might actually get in a way (happen I decide to make a view of the annexed files based on some meta-data field which gets aggregated and then present in metadata for that file?)\n\n- I would also prefer to have a bit more descriptive name than just `info`, e.g. if it is aggregated meta-data -- call it so, i.e. `aggregated`.\n\n2. `.datalad/meta/objects`\n -  not sure what those `categorylabel` would be needed for, and how 'cleansing' would happen (upon reaggregation remove previous hashes?) to keep it all reasonable\n - yet to understand this hole scheme... I guess some specific example/drawing sketch could've helped\n\n3. `helpers`\n  - before all the fanciness, I am in a dire need for a basic  dataset metadata  entry helper.  ATM establishing even basic meta-data for the dataset is a dark magic.  I don't care what format it would be in, or how entered... may be it could be that we just provide a template with descriptive comments (which would be ignored when saving actual result, but better format allows for comments), so when people run smth like `datalad metadata --edit`, it would e.g. copy the template, and fire up editor, and when done (exit editor) would validate that it is all kosher, and if not -- alert to problems and provide an option to edit again, and when succeeded to be clean, aggregate/save it right away.  Would be tremendously useful.\n  - assigning tags based on some filename regexps might indeed be cool/useful. We should provide clear feedback though on what files got what flags to help prevent marking files incorrectly (e.g. assigning some tag which would \"facilitate\" public publishing of those files, whenever they might should have not been published publicly)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1491380018,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI5MTc4NzQyNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-291787427"},"message":"\u003e scalability issue: annex will assign those aggregated fields to the 'key' of that meta-data file. If that file to change more or less frequently, its key would be changing, meta-data would need to be duplicated/expanded for the the new key.\n\nGood point. So we should have a third file whose content does not change unless the datasets' own basic metadata changes. Maybe we simply put a dataset's basic metadata in this file which solves the where-to-put-this problem. On caching/aggregation annex meta data is updated from this file. So only a change in meta data will cause a change in the key, and thereby justify an updated metadata set for the new key.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1500045981,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMxNTM4ODc4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1287#issuecomment-315388782"},"message":"Most of this has been implemented one way or the other in #1630. Closing.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1500045981,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MTE2NDQ3NTk2Mg=="},"status":2},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1500046016,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDExNjQ0NzY5MTc="},"added":["fix-implemented"],"removed":[]},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1500046016,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTE2NDQ3NjkxOA=="},"added":[],"removed":["feedback-desired"]}]}